    "title": "Initial Reports Shed Light on Victor Wembanyama's Apparent Knee Injury - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenny Nosay ,\n40 minutes ago\nVictor Wembanyama (Image Credits: Imagn) San Antonio Spurs superstar Victor Wembanyama is down again due to an injury.\nSince arriving in the league in 2023, basketball fans have yet to see Wemby play for an entire season. The highest number of games he played happened during his rookie year, which is seventy-one. After that, he’s been in and out due to various ailments. Understandably, the Spurs are overly cautious about his health .\nAgainst the New York Knicks, the 7-foot-5 big man went down with an apparent knee injury. Thankfully, this time, he only suffered a slight hyperextension in his left knee and avoided another major setback.\n“Spurs star Victor Wembanyama suffered a slight hyperextension in his left knee in tonight’s win over New York — and initial tests came back negative and showed no major injury,” per ESPN’s Shams Charania.\nThis is good news for San Antonio. While it’s to be expected that Wemby might miss some games, at least his tests were good and he avoided another serious injury. There’s no doubt that they are a much better team with him on the floor.\nVictor Wembanyama Opens Up About Health Scare Victor Wembanyama (Image Credits: Imagn) Last season, Victor Wembanyama only appeared in 46 games due to a career-threatening blood clot , which was discovered after February’s All-Star break. He was playing at an MVP level during that time before his season was cut short.\nFor a young guy like him, having one of basketball’s most unfortunate injuries affected how he viewed his personal life. Almost a year after it happened, he talked about his thought process about his health scare.\n“It’s gonna be one year soon since I learned,” Wembanyama said. “And it was five minutes of total breakdown. Praying and sadness, and feeling the fragility of life.”\nHopefully, he stays healthy throughout his career. One day, should he continue his stellar play, the league will be his.\nThe post Initial Reports Shed Light on Victor Wembanyama’s Apparent Knee Injury originally published on Total Pro Sports .",
